Facts from other projects
-------------------------

TP-Link does not publish these protocols. The facts this module uses
(ports, framing, the XOR obscuring, the KLAP handshake and auth hashes,
the securePassthrough exchange and login, the discovery probe on 20002,
method and field names, error codes, per-model colour-temperature ranges)
were read from public descriptions, chiefly python-kasa
(github.com/python-kasa/python-kasa, GPL-3.0). python-kasa is a
GPL-licensed project: no code was taken from it, and nothing in this
module is a translation of it; only facts were used. Since v0.2.0 the
fields of the Tapo energy history request were also read from
fabiankachlock/tapo-api (MIT) and mihai-dinculescu/tapo (MIT), and the
name of the Kasa countdown module confirmed in cloudkucooland/go-kasa
(BSD-2-Clause), as facts only; no code was taken. Since v0.3.0 the
request names and fields of Tapo schedule and countdown writes and of
camera requests were also read from mihai-dinculescu/tapo (MIT),
JurajNyiri/pytapo (MIT) and petretiandrea/plugp100 (GPL-3.0), as facts
only; no code was taken. The AES-CCM cipher follows RFC 3610. See
PROVENANCE.md.

Credentials
-----------

The module contains no credential: no vendor setup account, no camera
default login, no key and no account of the author or of any user.
KLAPAuthsWith and AESLoginsWith take any further accounts to try from the
caller; the camera clients take the device's user and password from the
caller.

Interop tests (interop/, a separate test-only module)
-----------------------------------------------------

interop/peer/Dockerfile installs python-kasa 0.11.0.1 (GPL-3.0) from
PyPI and downloads the recorded device fixtures of its 0.11.0.1 tag into
a python:3.12.10-slim image at test time; nothing of python-kasa is
copied into this repository, and it is not linked with this module.
interop/peer/device.py is our own script that calls python-kasa. The
expected values in sslaes_test.go were computed by python-kasa's
functions from made-up inputs (facts about its output, not its code).

